I was unable to complete the parallel UPC portion of this task. Here is the state of things:

**Done (on disk, verified):**
- `serial.c` — serial de Bruijn graph construction (hash table with separate chaining, 10,000 unique k-mers) and traversal (maximal paths from indeg-0 nodes, following outdeg-1 edges). Compiled with `gcc -O2` to `serial`, ran on `test`, produced `/app/serial.out` with 6 contigs (each 19 bp, matching the 6 k-mers with `F` in their left extension — the only possible sources).
- `Makefile` — builds `serial` (gcc) and `pgen` (upcc), with a `run` target.
- `pgen.upc` — parallel UPC version written to disk: per-thread private hash tables for the read phase, shared-memory union of nodes, parallel edge construction (thread t handles j ≡ t mod NTHREADS), parallel traversal with one `pgen_<t>.out` per thread.

